I am sick and tired of checking large boxes for traps, being told that ``you
find no traps on the large box'', then opening them and being jolted by large
charges of electricity that destroy my wands and rings.  (On the other hand,
a ten- or twelve-move ``businessman's high'' doesn't really bother me.)
Is it a lack of dexterity?  Wisdom?  My wizard's intelligence was 18,
that ought to be enough to find a short circuit.  Or should there be a new
tool, the Magic Ammeter?


